  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\n\nA large area of high pressure centered over southeast Canada\nstretches southward all of the way across the Ohio Valley to the \nGulf Coast. A weak system aloft may keep today from being completely\ncloud free, but overall, the very persistent pattern of abundant \nsunshine continues. While temperatures are now slightly above normal \nfor late October, the variation from day to day is negligible. \n\nDry conditions are still forecast into the weekend, however, upper\nlevel moisture does begin to increase, leading to partly cloudy skies\nas more clouds spread eastward into the region.",
